{
	"name": "Forest Gnome",
	"type": "culture",
	"img": "icons/environment/wilderness/tree-spruce.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Characters raised in the forest gnome culture share a variety of traits in common with one another.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Artistic Pursuits.</em></strong>&nbsp;You have proficiency in one type of artisans&rsquo; tools of your choice.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Natural Illusionist.&nbsp;</em></strong>You can cast @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.vemj08hawvmf44ya]{disguise self} once per long rest. Once you reach 3rd level, you can cast @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.250c4t64865s83si]{blur} once per long rest. At 5th level, you can cast @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.eceeym81z9dq6r58]{major image} once per long rest. You don&rsquo;t need material components for these spells, and when casting them your&nbsp;spellcasting&nbsp;ability is Intelligence or Wisdom (whichever is higher).</p><p><strong><em>Small Beast Speech.&nbsp;</em></strong>You have an innate ability to communicate simple thoughts and ideas with beasts of size Small or smaller.</p><p><strong><em>Languages.&nbsp;</em></strong>You can speak, read, write, and sign Common and Gnomish.</p>",
